%%{init: {"sequence": {"actorMargin": 70}}}%%
sequenceDiagram
    accTitle: What happens when the desktop quits or the user revokes access
    accDescr: Two cases. If the user quits the Companion, existing traffic can keep renewing leases but no fresh handshake can be signed. If the user revokes, the Broker records it, refuses further renewal, and the Gateway closes both sockets by the current lease deadline.
    participant C as Companion
    participant B as Broker
    participant G as Gateway
    Note over C,G: A connection already has a valid grant and traffic leases
    rect {band-request}
    Note over C,G: Case 1: the user quits the Companion
    C--xB: Signing channel closes
    G->>B: Renew for existing traffic
    B-->>G: Lease within grant expiry
    Note over C,G: A fresh handshake needs the approving Companion back online
    end
    rect {band-sign}
    Note over C,G: Case 2: the user revokes access
    C->>B: Request revocation once online
    B-->>C: Revocation recorded
    B-->>G: Retirement notice, if delivered
    G->>B: Next renewal, if notice lost
    B-->>G: Refused
    Note over B,G: Close both sockets by the current lease deadline
    end
